Provenance
----------

Thanks to kashakov, who helped work out the GC protobufs, and to itsjfx's
node-dota2-user (GPL-3.0), whose behaviour this library re-implements
independently under MIT. Protobuf definitions come from SteamDatabase/Protobufs
and originate from Valve's Dota 2 client.

No source code was copied from node-dota2-user. Its observable behaviour — the
hello/welcome handshake, the connection-status driven reconnect and the shape of
the message router — was studied and re-implemented from scratch.

The files under src/protobufs are machine-generated by protoc + ts-proto from the
.proto definitions published at https://github.com/SteamDatabase/Protobufs, which
are extracted from Valve's Dota 2 client. They describe Valve's wire format and
carry no copyright claim by this project.

